{"title":"","link":"http://scripting.com/2026/06/01.html#a204534","date":1780346734000,"content":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_C._Reilly\">John C Reilly</a> has only one audiobook, <a href=\"https://www.audible.com/pd/One-Flew-Over-the-Cuckoos-Nest-Audiobook/B008N1TVDU?qid=1780346782&amp;sr=1-1&amp;ref_pageloadid=not_applicable&amp;pf_rd_p=83218cca-c308-412f-bfcf-90198b687a2f&amp;pf_rd_r=WW3M8GMMBTRYDR07EKF2&amp;plink=VOtUYOmY1vBkYr5V&amp;pageLoadId=BtEBBZapmpvZd7IT&amp;creativeId=0d6f6720-f41c-457e-a42b-8c8dceb62f2c&amp;ref=a_search_c3_lProduct_1_1\">One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest</a>. But it's the best audiobook I've ever read, because the narrator and the book are great, esp together. Wish he would do more. Also there's a <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2026/05/28/nx-s1-5836617/john-c-reilly-mr-romantic\">great interview</a> with him on the Rachel Martin <a href=\"https://feedland.com/?feedurl=https%3A%2F%2Ffeeds.npr.org%2F510379%2Fpodcast.xml#\">podcast</a>.","author":"","siteTitle":"Scripting News","siteHash":"d6ad59631287cc248e52fdfe0c4f962c0fd08643d455b40f799700d8b2f97c65","entryHash":"bd01b9bcc72ee0d4b21c1f1a6cb49e4eec78250158d99fad88554c443354997a","category":"Sites"}